From 022fa92e394f0b15841c26890be8772d983b28d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:17:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nxp-nci: unregister without holding the mode mutex

Carry the reviewed change into the maintained LTS tree. Preserve the
original author, timestamp, source notices and assistance disclosures.
Keep the existing LTS allocation, I2C ID and NCI interfaces. The
optional clock reconciliation omits newer-base cleanup already absent
from LTS.

The actual NCI close/reset/receive/removal model reproduces nine wrong
baseline cases and none of ten after repair. Nine optional-clock/probe
cases and nine teardown/clock regression variants pass their
contracts. WCNSS selection/classification is already present and
tested separately. Sixty ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT native objects
compile without diagnostics using nonpermissive CFI, including
built-in/module and ACPI-off/on paths. All nineteen family DTBs pass
the full schema; sixteen remain identical, and the three Madai
variants gain only NFC and its bus/pin configuration. Seventy-five
inherited DTC warnings are retained without a new diagnostic.

Core services, locks, IRQ completion, bus, clocks and scheduling are
modeled. Physical NFC/radio, concurrent firmware, complete driver core
and final-image qualification remain open. Codex prepared the LTS port
and qualification. Human DCO and owner/security review remain pending;
no sign-off, phone action, Wi-Fi scan or publication is claimed.

Original reviewed changelog and disclosures:

Removing an open controller calls nci_unregister_device(), which
closes the NCI device and invokes nxp_nci_close(). That callback takes
info_lock, but nxp_nci_remove() already holds the same mutex across
unregister. The recursive acquisition prevents removal from
completing.

Unregister without info_lock held, then set the transport and driver
mode to cold under the mutex. Release the mutex before freeing the NCI
device. Keep the existing firmware-work shutdown sequence unchanged.

Fixes: dece45855a8b ("NFC: nxp-nci: Add support for NXP NCI chips") The original draft disclosed generic LLM assistance.

Ported to the current NFC maintainer tree with OpenAI Codex
assistance. Original implementation commits and author timestamps are
retained in the review evidence. Synthetic lifecycle tests reproduce
the locking and IRQ ordering paths; physical NFC and concurrent
firmware acceptance remain open. Human review and DCO certification
are pending.

Backported from commit 87b848f087e6 ("nfc: nxp-nci: unregister without
holding the mode mutex")
---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
index 66b198663387a..87a7bbf4d4a49 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
@@ -185,15 +185,15 @@ void nxp_nci_remove(struct nci_dev *ndev)
 		nxp_nci_fw_work_complete(info, -ESHUTDOWN);
 	cancel_work_sync(&info->fw_info.work);
 
-	mutex_lock(&info->info_lock);
+	nci_unregister_device(ndev);
 
+	mutex_lock(&info->info_lock);
 	if (info->phy_ops->set_mode)
 		info->phy_ops->set_mode(info->phy_id, NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD);
+	info->mode = NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD;
+	mutex_unlock(&info->info_lock);
 
-	nci_unregister_device(ndev);
 	nci_free_device(ndev);
-
-	mutex_unlock(&info->info_lock);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(nxp_nci_remove);
 
